  "firstCustomInput": "expiryDate",
  "firstRuleChain": "",
  "ruleSetPolicy": "",
  "description": "In a pharmacy or an online medical store, medicines should not be sold if they are expired. This rule ensures that customers only receive valid medicines and helps avoid health hazards. The system should check the expiry date of a medicine and block its sale if it has expired or is within a certain threshold before expiry (e.g., X days before the expiry date).\n\nAdditionally, special conditions can apply:\n\nIf a medicine expires within 30 days, it should be marked as \"Near Expiry\" and sold at a discount (if allowed).\nIf a medicine expires within 7 days, it should be removed from sale.\nIf a medicine is already expired, it should be blocked completely.",
